## 3. Enlarge the actual hit areas of the 18px icons

The governing criterion is **2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum), Level AA**. Pointer targets normally need space for a **24 × 24 CSS-pixel** square, but WCAG provides several exceptions. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="14"}

[W3C — Understanding 2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum)](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/target-size-minimum?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

First measure the **clickable/tappable target**, not the artwork. An 18×18 icon inside a 32×32 or 44×44 button has no 18px target-size problem.

If the actual targets are 18×18 and directly adjacent, however, they are likely to fail. WCAG permits undersized controls when there is sufficient clearance: conceptually, center a 24 CSS-pixel diameter circle on each undersized target; those circles must not intersect another target or the corresponding circle of another undersized target. W3C demonstrates that 20×20 controls with a 4px gap can pass, while 20×20 controls with no gap fail. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="16"}

The other exceptions are material:

- an equivalent conforming control performs the same function;
- the target is inline in text or constrained by text line height;
- its size comes from an unmodified user agent;
- that particular presentation is essential or legally required. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="17"}

For ordinary checkout icon buttons, most of those exceptions are unlikely.

**Two-week fix:** enlarge the **interactive button box**, not necessarily the visual icon, to at least 24×24 CSS px. For important checkout controls I would use a larger internal design-system minimum where layout permits; 24px is a WCAG floor, not a usability optimum. If changing the hit area is difficult, sufficient spacing can technically satisfy AA, but larger targets are less fragile.

W3C also documents using minimum container dimensions to ensure spacing. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="18"}

[W3C — C42: min-height/min-width for target spacing](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Techniques/css/C42?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

**Acceptance test:** inspect the computed target bounding box for every icon button at each breakpoint. For each one either establish ≥24×24 CSS px or explicitly document which exception applies and verify its geometry.

