# E. Contradictions and alternative explanations

Several apparent contradictions disappear once the exact criteria are separated.

**“The footer overlaps focus, therefore it fails AA.”** Not necessarily: 2.4.11 permits partial obscuring. Entire obscuring is the relevant AA failure; zero obscuring is AAA. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="36"}

**“The icons are 18px, therefore they fail.”** Not necessarily: the visible icon and the interactive target may have different dimensions. Also, undersized targets can sometimes pass by spacing or another exception. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="37"}

**“The slider works with arrow keys, so it is accessible.”** That may satisfy the keyboard aspect but still fail 2.5.7 because that criterion exists specifically for pointer users who cannot perform dragging. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="38"}

**“Browser autofill solves the repeated address.”** W3C explicitly says it does not satisfy 3.3.7 by itself. Site-provided reuse of information from the current process is required. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="39"}

